Build is clean (0 warnings, 0 errors). Here's a summary of all breaking changes identified and fixed:

---

### Breaking changes fixed in this project

| # | Breaking Change | Fix Applied |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **TFM & packages** → `net8.0`/EF 8.0 | Updated to `net9.0` / EF Core `9.0.0` |
| 2 | **`HasData` with `DateTime.UtcNow`** — non-deterministic seed data causes `Migrate()` to throw "pending model changes" | Replaced with fixed constant `new DateTime(2024, 1, 1, …, DateTimeKind.Utc)` |
| 3 | **`Migrate()` inside explicit transaction** — EF Core 9 now manages its own transactions and throws if wrapped | Removed `CreateExecutionStrategy`/`BeginTransaction` wrapper; `Migrate()` is called directly |
| 4 | **`Design` package not found** (SDK ≥ 9.0.200) — private assets excluded from `.deps.json` | Added `<Publish>true</Publish>` and explicit `<IncludeAssets>` |

### Cosmos DB breaking changes (for your separate project)

You mentioned a Cosmos DB project with existing documents. Apply these fixes in its `OnModelCreating`:

```csharp
// 1. Preserve old discriminator name (default changed to "$type")
modelBuilder.Entity<YourEntity>().HasDiscriminator<string>("Discriminator");

// 2. Preserve old compound id format ("EntityType|Key" → just "Key")
modelBuilder.Entity<YourEntity>().HasRootDiscriminatorInJsonId(true);

// 3. Replace ALL sync calls — Cosmos provider now throws on sync I/O
//    ToList()       → await ToListAsync()
//    SaveChanges()  → await SaveChangesAsync()
//    First()        → await FirstAsync()
```

Also remove any `HasIndex()` calls on Cosmos entities — they now throw at startup.
